---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="How ServerPulse is built – Astro, performance and SEO"
  description="A short write-up of how ServerPulse was built with Astro: static HTML, one small script, and the SEO basics."
>
  <h1>How it's built</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    ServerPulse is a small project I built to learn Astro and to practise
    web performance and SEO on something gamers would actually use.
  </p>

  <h2>Static first</h2>
  <p>
    Every page is generated as plain HTML at build time. The server cards come from
    one data file, so adding a server is a one-line change. There is no UI framework
    in the browser.
  </p>

  <h2>One small script</h2>
  <p>
    The only JavaScript on the site is a short file that asks the public
    mcsrvstat.us API for each server's status and fills in the cards. If it fails,
    the page still reads fine and the card says “No data”.
  </p>

  <h2>Performance choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>System fonts, so there is no font download.</li>
    <li>No images apart from an SVG icon.</li>
    <li>CSS written by hand and shipped with the page.</li>
    <li>Layout that works from phone width up, with no horizontal scroll.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>SEO basics</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A unique title and description on every page.</li>
    <li>Canonical URLs and Open Graph tags.</li>
    <li>A generated sitemap and a robots.txt that points to it.</li>
    <li>Semantic HTML: one h1 per page, labelled form fields, real landmarks.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Source</h2>
  <p>
    The code is on <a href="https://github.com/JBWeb1">my GitHub</a>.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  p, li { max-width: 65ch; }
  ul { padding-left: 20px; }
</style>
